  "description": "Reid Bikes ATB | 26\" mountain bike\nA practical, dependable mountain bike for everyday cycling – the Reid Bikes ATB combines a durable steel frame, versatile gearing and easy-to-maintain components for exploring paths, trails and local routes.\nThe Reid Bikes ATB is an entry-level mountain bike designed for riders looking for a reliable bike for everyday adventures and recreational cycling. Featuring a durable Hi-Tensile steel frame and 26\" wheels, it offers a straightforward, easy-to-use setup for exploring local paths, riding around town and discovering light off-road routes.\nA rigid steel fork keeps the design simple and low-maintenance, while 680mm alloy riser handlebars and a matching 60mm stem provide comfortable steering and control. The 26 x 1.95\" all-terrain tyres offer predictable handling across a range of surfaces, while double-wall alloy rims add durability for regular riding.\nA 3x7-speed drivetrain, featuring Shimano Tourney front and TY300 rear derailleurs, provides 21 gearing options to help tackle hills and enjoy flatter routes. Alloy V-brakes offer straightforward stopping power, while a sealed bottom bracket and comfortable MTB saddle complete the practical setup.\nWhether you're exploring local paths, heading out on weekend rides or looking for a straightforward introduction to off-road cycling, the Reid Bikes ATB offers dependable performance and practical versatility.\nThe Reid Bikes ATB is ideal for:\n\nEntry-level mountain bike riders, looking for a straightforward introduction to off-road cycling\n\nEveryday recreational riding, with a durable Hi-Tensile steel frame and practical components\n\nExploring paths and light trails, with 26\" wheels and 1.95\" all-terrain tyres\n\nRiders looking for versatile gearing, with a 3x7-speed drivetrain offering 21 gear options\n\nSimple, easy-to-maintain cycling, with a rigid steel fork and dependable alloy V-brakes\n\nComfortable everyday riding, with 680mm alloy handlebars and an MTB comfort saddle\n\nRegular recreational use, with double-wall alloy rims and a sealed bottom bracket",
